        "sha256:1c821a7d5ed8aec96fbd1a777f853b0e482a8c2f9b76373df3dc2c6f51af6661"
      ],
      "reason": "The prohibition of any test suite, build, failure investigation or landing step in the Architect's own chat is replaced by a bounded freedom: he may check, measure, run, read and try things on a copy, that work never substitutes for a leaf's build, review, curation or gate, and his only landing step stays the paired-closeout exception with the added statement that a check before a landing is not a step of it. The two realizations and the closeout proof are re-anchored on the final bytes; RLZ-1GCP9C at roles/architect.md:54 states the new rule, and the kept closeout sentence it preserves is still proved by PRF-H64HF6. Evidence (MIK-R184@v1/A1/CODE-R1): A1-route-doctrine.md; A1-route-budgets.md; A1-route-regressions.md; focused-tests.txt (64 passed,642 subtests); wording-control.txt; a1-inspection.json; A1-onboarding-context.md identifies pending memory work",
